{#
  T-4.06b — the shoppable lookbook section on Home.

  This template is almost nothing, and that is the point. Everything that makes a
  hotspot work lives in `components.ui.hotspot-image`, because the owner's B6
  ruling says one component serves T-4.06 and T-7.07 and a second implementation
  is a defect. This registers the section, hands the merchant's settings over, and
  stops.

  | Variable                  | Type    | Description                              |
  |---------------------------|---------|------------------------------------------|
  | component.image           | string  | The editorial photograph                 |
  | component.alt             | ?string | Empty means decorative                   |
  | component.layout          | string  | `overlay` or `list`                      |
  | component.hotspots[].x    | int     | 0–100, a PERCENTAGE                      |
  | component.hotspots[].y    | int     | 0–100, a PERCENTAGE                      |
  | component.hotspots[].product_id | string | Resolved at runtime, never stored   |
  | position                  | int     | Sorting number, from zero                |

  ONE SECTION IS ONE IMAGE, AND THE MERCHANT ADDS IT TWICE. The artboard shows
  two shoppable blocks on Home with different layouts, so the alternative shape —
  a collection of images each holding a collection of points — would need a
  nested collection, which the manifest schema does not support. One image per
  section is simpler for the merchant and needs no feature the platform lacks.
#}
{% if component.image and component.hotspots|length %}
    <section data-testid="store-home-lookbook" class="s-block lookbook container">
        {% include 'components.ui.hotspot-image' with {
            image:    component.image,
            alt:      component.alt,
            layout:   component.layout,
            hotspots: component.hotspots,
            id:       'lookbook-' ~ position
        } %}
    </section>
{% endif %}
